ionClaim`); D2 by `runtimeSourceOf` and `runtimeSourceAmong`; the refusal test asserts the resume's own wording (`then resume again`). `TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim`, `TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession` and `TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath` fail with each guard mutated out (the recorded name, the thread's source, the name's path, the exclusive take, the verb).\n \n ### Results summary\n+The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n+- R2 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession\n+- R3 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession\n+- R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n \n ### Known gaps\n+None.\n \n ## 7. Final Report\n \n ### Delivered scope\n+A continuation takes the attempt's runtime directory before its claim, and every continuation, including a run from an earlier engine and a round continuing its thread, recreates the checkout under the name its session saw.\n \n ### Files and modules changed\n+`pose-mcp` review dispatch, resume and handoff plans, and their tests.\n \n ### Validation executed\n+`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n \n ### Residual risks\n+L1 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-Origin: `pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout` (done 2026-11-26).\n+None. Origin: `pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout` (done 2026-11-26).\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\nindex 414ace8f..9ea10c6c 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n@@ -317,7 +317,7 @@ func TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath(t *testin\n \tif err := os.Mkdir(runtimeDir, 0o700); err != nil {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n-\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"resume\", prior.RunID); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"still exists\") {\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"resume\", prior.RunID); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"then resume again\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"a resume beside a leftover runtime directory: %d %s\", code, out)\n \t}\n \t// Review round 2, N6: a handoff is refused the same way, before it\n@@ -328,6 +328,23 @@ func TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath(t *testin\n \tif err := os.Remove(runtimeDir); err != nil {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n+\t// Spec pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups R1: a directory that\n+\t// appears between the plan and the dispatch is refused before the claim,\n+\t// so the interrupted run stays resumable.\n+\tstore := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n+\tplan, err := store.PlanReviewResume(prior.RunID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.Mkdir(runtimeDir, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := store.RunReviewDispatch(plan, time.Now); err == nil || !(strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"already exists\") || strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"still exists\")) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a dispatch beside a directory that appeared: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.Remove(runtimeDir); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n \tcode, out := runPose(t, root, \"delegate\", \"resume\", prior.RunID)\n \tif code != 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"status=completed\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the resumed session did not find its checkout at %s: %d %s\", checkout, code, out)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\nindex c5b6278b..c157a8cb 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go